per using Claude Code skills**, I want to **backlog_normalize: add tags={\\\"admin\\\"} to hide from default tool pickers** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: fastmcp-creator skill analysis of backlog_core/server.py\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-07\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-23)\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- [ ] `backlog_normalize` tool decorator reads `@mcp.tool(tags={\\\"admin\\\"})` in `server.py`\\n- [ ] MCP tool listing filtered by tags={\\\"admin\\\"} returns backlog_normalize; unfiltered listing omits it (verify via fastmcp list)\\n- [ ] `uv run ruff check plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` exits 0\\n- [ ] Existing backlog_normalize behavior unchanged\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` \u2014 `@mcp.tool()` decorator on `backlog_normalize`\\n\\n### Story\\n\\nAs an **MCP client tool picker showing available tools**, I want **`backlog_normalize` tagged as `admin`** so that **it doesn't appear in standard tool lists alongside operational tools like `backlog_add` and `backlog_view`**.\\n\",\"digest\":\"4093eb914af70a88702fea3aed5920b4273a2516e379cce641369cd8d34feb3d\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPg0W2Q\"}"}